          "source_pointer": "/common_specification/model/description_paragraphs/0",
          "source_value": "The public feasible set is the Euclidean ball $Q=B_2(0,D)=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^d:\\|x\\|_2\\le D\\}$. The unknown differentiable $f:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R$ has an $L$-Lipschitz gradient on the full space. At least one global minimizer is in $Q$, and the set $S=\\arg\\min_{x\\in Q} f(x)$ is convex.",
